    "output": "Entire's CLI is the source of truth for its own usage. Do not guess flags or\nsubcommands \u2014 read them from this command. You are already inside the repo:\nentire auto-detects it from the git origin remote, so never ask the user for the\nrepo name. Pass --repo only to target a DIFFERENT repo.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/neatlogs/neatlogs  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nWhen to use entire \u2014 the commands that bear on the work:\n  checkpoint  Inspect and search checkpoints\n                read-only except: explain\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n                read-only\n  session     Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n                read-only except: adopt, attach, resume, stop\n  status      Show Entire status\n                read-only\n  why         Show why a line exists\n                read-only\n\nAlso available (entire agent-help <command> for any of these):\n  read-only, safe to run:\n    activity \u00b7 labs \u00b7 recap \u00b7 version\n  when the task needs them:\n    api \u00b7 dispatch \u00b7 doctor\n  the user's \u2014 suggest, don't run:\n    agent \u00b7 auth \u00b7 clean \u00b7 cluster \u00b7 configure \u00b7 disable \u00b7 enable\n    login \u00b7 logout \u00b7 org \u00b7 plugin \u00b7 project \u00b7 repo\n\nDrill in for exact, currently-installed flags:  entire agent-help <command>  (e.g. entire agent-help checkpoint)\nAdd --json for structured output."
